This directory holds the project's private libraries. Each one is an ESP-IDF
component: lib/<Name>/ has a CMakeLists.txt that calls idf_component_register(),
its sources in src/, a README.md (purpose, maturity, dependencies, consumers,
tests, open items) and a REFERENCE.md (API, tasks and timing, AppConfig keys,
errors, console commands, usage).

The firmware project picks them up through EXTRA_COMPONENT_DIRS in
idf/CMakeLists.txt, and idf/main/CMakeLists.txt lists them in REQUIRES. A
component exposes its headers through INCLUDE_DIRS and names its own
dependencies in REQUIRES.

  AppConfig      Stored runtime parameters: one NVS set, the schema, cfg/TFT access
  BootLogRing    Keeps the first log output after reset for the bootlog command
  CellNetL2      Raw-Ethernet (0x88B5) cell messages, transports, OTA receiver
  EtherNetIP     EtherNet/IP and CIP originator: codecs, Class 1 scanner tasks
  EthernetLink   LAN8720 bring-up, static IP or DHCP, link events
  Gantry         The motion API: Kinetix X/Z and HCS01 theta axes, homing, paths
  GantryOta      Firmware updates into the passive OTA slot, over TCP or CellNet
  GpioExpander   Field I/O, encoder, TFT lines and W5500 reset on the MCP23S17
  MCP23S17       Driver for the MCP23S17 SPI GPIO expander
  Spi3Bus        Owns SPI3 (MCP23S17 and TFT) and the Class 1 critical section
  SpiDisplay     ST7789 TFT and its menu UI
  ThetaTrace     1 kHz theta move trace and its summary (thtrace)
  W5500          W5500 driver on SPI2: init, recovery, sockets, bus mutex

Build the whole project from the repo root:
  idf.py -C idf build

All documents are listed in docs/INDEX.md; the build and test workflow is in
CONTRIBUTING.md.
